  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "gr-noni",
  "connector": "〜のに",
  "gloss": "even though (and that’s annoying)",
  "title": "〜のに — even though, and yet",
  "pattern": "plain form + のに (noun / な-adjective + なのに)",
  "explanation": "のに joins two things that clash, usually with surprise, regret or complaint: {頑張|がんば}ったのに、だめだった — I tried so hard, and still it didn’t work. {日曜日|にちようび}なのに、{仕事|しごと}だ — it’s Sunday, and I’m working. On its own at the end, it’s a sigh: {言|い}ったのに… — but I told you…",
  "natural": "For complaints and regrets in conversation. けど is the neutral “but”; のに adds the feeling.",
  "stiff": "のに can’t be followed by a request or a suggestion: {雨|あめ}なのに、{行|い}こう is wrong. Use けど: {雨|あめ}だけど、{行|い}こう.",
